# `-d share` only — the SHARE-backed LIBRARY on the Unraid box.
# Read as [.kamal/secrets-common, .kamal/secrets.share].
#
# NO STORAGE CREDENTIAL OF ITS OWN. A share container holds no storage credential: its library is a
# mounted directory at LIBRARY_PATH, so there is nothing to sign for. config/deploy.share.yml
# re-declares env.secret as [RAILS_MASTER_KEY] precisely to DROP the chunk secret it would
# otherwise inherit, and RAILS_MASTER_KEY plus the registry password both come from
# .kamal/secrets-common.
#
# This file used to be empty on exactly that argument, and it still would be if `env.secret` were
# the whole story. It is not, since Arc D Task 2: `accessories:` in config/deploy.yml is never
# overridden by any destination overlay, so the `sync` accessory's own SECRET_KEY_BASE/
# SYNC_ADMIN_TOKEN are folded into every destination's merged config, this one included — verified
# against Kamal::Configuration.raw_config, not assumed. SECRET_KEY_BASE lives in secrets-common (see
# that file's own comment: it is exactly TINKEREX_SYNC_DEPLOY_KEY's shape, needed identically
# everywhere). SYNC_ADMIN_TOKEN deliberately does NOT: it also has genuine per-destination meaning
# (only `remote`'s maker app actually SENDS it), so parking it in secrets-common would blur that —
# see the fuller comment in .kamal/secrets.remote, the one copy that is functionally exercised.
SYNC_ADMIN_TOKEN=$(bin/secret SYNC_ADMIN_TOKEN 'op://tinkerex/tinkerex-sync-admin-token/password')

# Add a genuinely share-specific credential HERE, not in secrets-common: everything in
# secrets-common is parsed and executed by every other destination too (§14g).
